  "result": "All 5 tests pass.\n\n**What I built:** `kvstore/store.py` implements `Store` as a single JSON object on disk. The file is loaded once on open and kept in memory. Every `set`, `delete`, and `close` rewrites the file atomically by writing to a temp file in the same directory, fsyncing, and renaming over the target, so a crash mid-write never leaves a corrupt data file. Values are written with `ensure_ascii=False` so Unicode stays readable, and keys are sorted in the file for stable diffs. Beyond the required interface, the class supports use as a context manager, plus `len()` and `in`.\n\n**Approach chosen:** Approach A, the JSON document file. The spec targets a tiny CLI store where human readability and trivial inspection matter more than scale, and JSON satisfies the single-file constraint most cleanly, whereas SQLite leaves journal or WAL side files alongside the database during and sometimes after use.",
